<http://data.silknow.org/object/43e84962-dd04-3056-8013-32a4cb2547e2/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Workbox of rosewood, rectangular in shape, slightly tapering.  There is a raised, rectangular brass plaque in the centre of the hinged lid and the front is also inlaid with brass bands.  On each side is a wooden ring drop handle.  The box has four flat circular feet, and the whole is lined with blue silk.  Inside are bobbins, scissors, needles and various other sewing tools."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/43e84962-dd04-3056-8013-32a4cb2547e2> .

